Subject: [PATCH] Run 8: the accept and the server's hello time themselves
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run 8 (200 hellos and nothing else): accepting took 5.6 s for 100 at once
against 1.4 s alone, and the server's own greeting (no model) 2.5-3.8 s
against 0.5. The searches were not the cause, and the logs cannot say what
was: the host stamps them in batches (all 200 arrivals carry one
millisecond). So the process measures itself:

- [accept-timing] per accepted message: time from when this process first
  saw the request (a first middleware stamps it) to the handler, then each
  phase — thread lookup, title, payer, allowance and the 202 — and the total.
- [greeting] now says how long its reads and its save took.
- [loop-lag] reports a blocked event loop from 250 ms, not 2 s.

No behaviour changes.

